WEBVTT

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.400
Whoa, this soup is delicious!

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.600
I'm glad.

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:13.180
It wasn't a mix or anything, 
I actually made it from scratch!

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.850
Mommy's good at cooking, right?

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:17.030
Right!

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.570
<i>Because of me, 
Shinoaki lost her desire to draw,</i>

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:21.790
<i>and put down her pen.</i>

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.300
<i>She lost the future where 
she becomes Akishima Shino.</i>

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.290
<i>And yet...</i>

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.290
It's okay now.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.140
I'm sorry, Shinoaki.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.440
I'm so sorry.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.890
<i>To make sure her sacrifice wasn't in vain...</i>

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:41.220
<i>I have to live as best I can in this world 
that's so different from the one I know.</i>

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:45.230
<i>I'll do what I can, at least for now.</i>

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:49.230
<i>And carefully, so that I don't 
repeat the same mistake.</i>

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.620
Hashiba-san, can you check this?

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:27.610
What do you think?

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.920
The body should be good to go.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:33.870
But I think the cloth here might overlap with
 the other characters when they're lined up,

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.260
so make it a little smaller.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:36.080
Got it.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.770
And about the empty space for a symbol,

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:41.360
I had the design for that made separately, 
so just stick that in there.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.080
Wait, you did?

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:47.960
Yeah. It'll reduce the workload on 
the illustrators, and be easier to reuse.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:49.720
I should've known! That will be a big help.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:53.510
Hashiba-san, three of the backgrounds 
that were in the pipeline are ready.

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:55.390
Got it. I'll check them right now.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:58.480
The files are pretty big, 
so I put them in the shared folder.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.320
All right.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:03.320
Downloading 1 file...

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:03.320
10 minutes remaining

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:03.320
Pause

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:03.320
Cancel

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.320
<i>Huh, guess I'll respond to this email first.</i>

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:07.110
<i>It's been a month since 
I was sent into 2018,</i>

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.350
<i>and I'm finally starting 
to get used to my job.</i>

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:11.710
<i>From the information 
I grasped in the meantime,</i>

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:17.300
<i>Entertainment Group 3 
is working on social games.</i>

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.760
<i>We're split up into four teams, 
labeled A through D,</i>

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:23.010
<i>and each of us are working 
on different projects in parallel.</i>

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.440
<i>Kawasegawa is charge of the A Team,</i>

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.970
<i>which is the team everyone 
thinks of regarding this group.</i>

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:31.790
<i>She's the Chief of
 Entertainment Group 3, too,</i>

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:32.500
What are you doing?!

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.690
<i>which means she's got one rough job.</i>

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.690
Sorry! I'm sorry!

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.690
<i>As for me, I'm the leader of the B Team.</i>

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:40.010
<i>B Team is known for its consistency 
in making headway,</i>

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:41.720
<i>along with stable contributions 
in terms of revenue,</i>

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.240
<i>so we seem to get put onto projects 
that need a steady hand.</i>

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:47.930
<i>It was hard to figure out how to do 
a job I have no memories of,</i>

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:51.200
<i>but once I got used to it, 
it wasn't that hard.</i>

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.000
<i>It's not easy, but it's stable work.</i>

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:57.740
This is for the best, right?

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.930
Hey, Daddy, let's play! Come on!

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:06.460
Is it okay if I rest today?

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:08.810
That's boring!

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:12.140
Come on, Daddy! Daddy, let's go!

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:14.760
Maki, don't bother him after he said no.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.210
It's Sunday, so let him enjoy his rest.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:18.460
Don't wanna!

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.690
Maki, stop it!

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:24.320
Are you going to apologize to Mr. Bear?

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.130
I'm sorry.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.500
Now, listen, Maki...

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.220
Whether it's a stuffed animal 
or anything else,

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:36.120
all things people make 
have spirits in them.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.310
Spirits?

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.130
Yep.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:42.940
And those spirits care a whole bunch 
about all those creations.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:45.970
So if you throw one of them around,
 what will they think?

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:48.930
They'll be sad.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:50.300
Right?

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:54.250
So be sure to be nice to Mr. Bear, Maki.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:55.110
Okay.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:01.610
<i>All creations have a spirit in them, huh?</i>

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:05.030
<i>It's times like this that 
I'm sure the woman I'm looking at</i>

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:08.240
<i>is the same Shinoaki I knew.</i>

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:14.330
<i>I've got a warm home life here.</i>

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.870
Hey, why don't we go for a walk?

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:19.130
<i>But the brilliant light 
I used to look up to...</i>

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:17.730
Yeah!

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:19.650
Can I take Mr. Bear, too?

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:24.020
<i>There's no trace of the glamour 
of the Platinum Generation anymore.</i>

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:21.060
Of course!

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.390
Well, uh, our company

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:32.260
in keeping with our aim 
to go public next quarter,

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:37.950
<i>must absolutely ensure we hit 
our sales goal for this quarter.</i>

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:40.130
<i>In light of that, </i>Mystic Clockwork<i>,</i>

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:43.470
<i>the title that our company 
is betting its future on...</i>

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:45.070
<i>will require everyone's support</i>

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.290
<i>as we work towards its completion.</i>

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:48.240
<i>That is all.</i>

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:50.700
I feel terrible for them.

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:53.750
Team A's been working overnight again.

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.120
Is it really that bad?

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.960
Well, there's the problem 
with Minori Ayaka...

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:58.890
Right.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:02.770
But there are apparently other illustrators 
they haven't been able to contact.

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:04.090
It sounds like a disaster.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.670
They've had to cut characters 
that were previously in the planning,

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:09.310
which results in changes to the script.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:19.100
Is Minori-sensei still 
having trouble drawing?

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.210
Yes...

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:22.000
I just got an email from her

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.580
saying that she doubts she'll 
manage to meet the deadline,

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:26.290
no matter how much she works.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:30.370
I thought we had a good conversation 
with her the other day.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:32.790
It's not that she's slacking or anything!

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:35.120
But she didn't offer any other explanation.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.870
Yeah, and when an artist runs into a block,

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.590
they're usually 
the ones it bothers the most.

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:44.630
Right. I'm a little worried 
that she's letting it overwhelm her.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.630
That's strange.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:50.830
There's still no answer.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:52.990
Even though I arranged 
an appointment beforehand.

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:54.730
Should we wait a bit?

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:56.640
I'll try and ask her about it.

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:02.540
Excuse—

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:03.920
<i>Okay, I'll open it up!</i>

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:07.380
That was amazing, Hashiba-san!

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:09.130
She opened it as soon as she responded!

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:11.470
Yeah, but... wasn't that a little too fast?

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:13.260
Of course not!

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:16.340
She seems to be feeling well, 
so come on, let's go!

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:23.790
Hey, thanks for bringing—

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:34.680
Well...

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:39.400
I opened the door because I thought 
it was the deliveryman.

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.680
I thought it was odd, 
considering you let us in

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:44.110
before we told you who we were.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.330
I don't dress like this outside at all.

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:49.330
It's just something I mess 
around with at home.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.650
Every once and a while, that's all.

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:55.440
Well, sure, but... it really suits you well.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:58.620
Oh, thank you.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.620
This is kind of embarrassing!

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.100
I mean, you know what they say 
about a change of pace.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.670
I was just... really restless.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.630
So this is about 
the character designs, right?

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:11.510
Yes!

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:15.700
I'm sorry! It's exactly like 
I wrote in the email.

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:18.300
I've been trying to get things done, but...

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:21.020
I just... haven't been able to so far.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:27.110
I've been trying all kinds of things 
to motivate myself since we last talked,

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:30.940
but it's like none of it works... 
even dressing like this.

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:34.280
I just... can't find the right thing.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:40.240
You mean, you can't find the thing 
that you want to draw?

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.200
What about the illustration 
from the other day?

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:45.670
That's...

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:48.320
When you started creating art seriously,

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:51.760
you said that you were drawing with 
a style similar to an artist you idolized.

00:08:53.560 --> 00:09:00.030
Is there any chance that getting a look 
at their work might help you?

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:03.520
I'm sorry. Right now, I just... can't.

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:08.160
I'm seriously so sorry.

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:11.900
But... that's not the problem.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.850
Hashiba-san, I think 
that's enough for today.

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:17.660
Yeah... okay.

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:22.120
I'm sorry, Morishita-san. 
I'll try and figure something out.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.260
Right.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:27.540
There's something she mentioned before.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:29.950
The longer you continue in this work,

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:32.630
you're bound to get into a rut,

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:35.300
where you'll be completely 
unable to draw anything.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.860
And I guess now is that time.

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:41.360
Yes. But there was more to what she said...

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:43.810
Once you get the right trigger,

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:45.860
you're suddenly able to draw again,

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:48.270
like you were never blocked 
in the first place.

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:49.560
A trigger, huh...

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:53.990
For now, I think even being able to meet 
with her today was a big accomplishment!

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:55.570
Thank you so much.

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:56.780
Nah...

00:09:57.670 --> 00:10:00.570
<i>The expression I saw on
 Minori-sensei's face last time...</i>

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:03.040
There's an artist I used to idolize,

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.380
and this is their style.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:08.940
I seriously, seriously love their stuff!

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:10.960
<i>There has to be something to that.</i>

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:13.590
<i>Something that'll get her drawing again.</i>

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:16.900
<i>That's the impression that I got.</i>

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:20.930
Kawasegawa-kun, 
do you realize what you're saying?!

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:24.720
The characters designed by Minori Ayaka 
 are the headliners this time!

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.900
It's already been announced to the public.

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:29.060
Delays are out of the question!

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.750
<i>In the end, it was decided 
that Minori Ayaka's illustrations</i>

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:34.230
<i>wouldn't be ready in time for release.</i>

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:39.180
Team A is already running on fumes 
with little sleep and no time off...

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:41.320
Add this to it all, and I can't help 
but feel sorry for them.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:43.220
Is it really that bad?

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:44.370
Take a look here.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:49.410
<b>Delayed</b>

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:47.870
They're talking about releasing 
in a month, despite all this.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.090
They're going through hell.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:53.520
Not to mention this mandate that they do it 
on an internally developed engine.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.550
Look, just get it done! All right?!

00:10:57.350 --> 00:11:01.630
It's been a while since you last asked 
me to join you for lunch, hasn't it?

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:02.550
I guess.

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:06.310
We've both been busy lately.

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:10.690
You want to talk about my 
team's project, don't you?

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.660
W-Well... yeah.

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:15.800
I was looking at the progress sheet.

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.900
Things don't seem to be going very well.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:21.010
That's one way of putting it. 
Another is that we're doomed.

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:23.240
I'm tempted to fly the coop to Okinawa.

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:34.730
Wait, so <i>Mystic Clockwork</i> 
was originally a SucceedSoft title?

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:36.300
You didn't know that?

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.900
I mean, of course I did!

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.380
If it came from a major player like Succeed,

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.870
I bet all the pre-production materials 
were in good shape.

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:46.030
Wouldn't that make things relatively easier?

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:49.890
Everyone thought that, at first. But...

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:54.440
Get a load of the requests they sent in.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.360
These are all requests for different takes?

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:57.770
And there's a lot...

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.530
There wasn't a limit set on this 
kind of thing beforehand?

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:03.690
I wouldn't be in this mess if there were.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:06.070
By the time it was put into my lap,

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:08.910
the contract was already 
signed under these conditions.

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:13.120
And when you top it off with an 
independently-developed, internal engine...

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.750
Yeah. Yet another source of headaches.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:19.160
We don't have enough time 
to outsource anything,

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:22.760
and when there are errors in the engine, 
they rear their head in scripting, too.

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:27.130
Since the art assets are so late, 
we're still using placeholders...

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:29.140
Which means the presentation 
can't be finalized.

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:32.730
It's like we're making 
every possible mistake.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.720
Listen, Kawasegawa...

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:39.940
I know.

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:43.020
The release needs to be delayed 
or major changes need to be made,

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:45.920
one or the other, or there's 
going to be major fallout.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:46.820
Right?

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:48.500
But it's not happening.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:52.410
Things are already beyond my ability 
to make any kind of positive difference.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.390
Sorry for worrying you.

00:12:56.390 --> 00:12:58.710
But there's just... 
nothing that can be done.

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:01.130
Nothing... that can be done?

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.480
This isn't like you!

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:08.760
You've always tried to do your best, 
until the very last second!

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:13.320
You're right. Thank you.

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:16.440
But you're the only person 
who thinks that anymore.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:17.950
That's...

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:21.850
Sorry. I'm gonna head on back.

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:29.870
You just don't get it!

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:33.700
But sir, if they proceed at this rate, 
they game will have bugs,

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:36.300
which could lead to defects 
nobody's imagined.

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:38.940
You deal with bugs 
and defects as they pop up.

00:13:38.940 --> 00:13:41.040
That's the whole point of maintenance.

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:46.950
Look, I know that you need time 
to make something good.

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:49.720
But in this business, timing is everything!

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:51.350
And delaying the release 
is out of the question!

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:52.640
But—

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:52.640
Enough!

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:56.420
This period is going to be crucial 
for the company's trust going forward!

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:58.200
We're going to go public at the same time

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:01.000
as we release a big title 
 developed on an internal engine!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:04.690
You don't need to be a manager 
to understand how important this is!

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:13.080
But the engine isn't trustworthy. 
It might not even be practical.

00:14:15.690 --> 00:14:19.730
<i>Mystic Clockwork</i> will be 
released on schedule.

00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:21.330
It's set in stone.

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:28.020
Hashiba-kun...

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:33.000
This is Kawasegawa-kun's job.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.430
You need to focus on your own tasks.

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:37.840
Don't meddle where you're not needed.

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:43.650
Understand? I trust you.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:47.530
Right...

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:54.950
Don't meddle, huh?

00:14:56.090 --> 00:14:57.960
<i>Thinking about it now,</i>

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:02.500
<i>when I showed up in their lives 
ten years ago, I changed the world.</i>

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.450
<i>My friends, who were supposed to have become</i>

00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:06.210
<i>the stars known as 
the Platinum Generation...</i>

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:08.950
<i>lost their dreams because of me.</i>

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:10.970
<i>I might have been trying to help,</i>

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:16.470
<i>but my interference ended up taking 
something important from them.</i>

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.310
<b><u>From the Desk of Rokuonji Tsurayuki</u></b>

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.310
<b>Magic</b>

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:18.270
<i>And if that's the case...</i>

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:23.990
There's nothing that can be done.

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:30.490
<i>The month after that, </i>Mystic Clockwork<i>
 launched on schedule.</i>

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:32.280
Hey, did you play that already?

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:34.490
Yeah, I installed it, but...

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:36.370
<i>We were able to start the service,</i>

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:39.230
<i>but bugs started popping up, 
the server kept going down...</i>

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:40.880
<i>There was no shortage of issues.</i>

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:44.900
<i>The staff is working to put out fires, while
 still having little sleep and no days off,</i>

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:46.920
<i>but the problems are outpacing them.</i>

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.940
Plus, the characters 
by Minori Ayaka got delayed...

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:51.750
Which sucks all the wind 
out of my gacha sails.

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:53.860
Huh, really?

00:15:57.210 --> 00:16:00.140
<i>There's nothing that can be done.</i>

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:08.690
Hey, Mommy, draw a horse right here!

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:13.860
I'm sorry, but Mommy's 
not a very good artist.

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.910
Aw, come on!

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:19.490
I can't draw a horse right!

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:22.540
I'm making dinner right now, okay?

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:25.770
Okay, let Daddy draw it for you.

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:26.840
Yay!

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:28.750
I appreciate it, honey.

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:30.880
It's nothing. Don't worry.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:33.080
What kind of horse do you want?

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:35.680
<i>Shinoaki used to be able to 
draw anything incredibly well.</i>

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:34.020
A zebra!

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:35.690
A... zebra?

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:37.720
<i>Her art always pulsated with an energy</i>

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:40.960
<i>that made you feel like 
it could jump to life.</i>

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:45.240
<i>But now... she doesn't draw anymore.</i>

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:47.990
<i>Even when her beloved daughter asks her.</i>

00:16:47.990 --> 00:16:49.730
Looks weird!

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:51.710
Daddy, you suck!

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:52.900
You think?

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.580
Don't be like that, Maki.

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:57.060
Daddy was nice enough to draw one for you.

00:16:57.060 --> 00:16:58.370
But look!

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:00.960
Oh, that's a cute puppy!

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:03.280
Sorry, one sec.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:08.840
Hello, Morishita-san? I'm at home right now.

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:09.920
Did something happen?

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:13.180
Okay. Okay.

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:15.360
I understand.

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:16.470
Was that work?

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:18.660
Sorry. I need to step out.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:22.850
I'm so sorry to bother you on your day off!

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:24.240
So what's happened?

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:27.940
It seems that the gacha rates 
are varying from account to account!

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.980
Seriously?! That shouldn't be possible!

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:31.640
Yes, but...

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:35.260
Are you familiar with 
the voice actor, Suenomori Yuta?

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.030
<b>Suenomori Yuta
</b>My pulls on MySClo are going super well
 Done with a recording session so gacha time!
 #MysticClockwork #MysClo

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:39.840
<i>It all began when the voice actor who 
portrayed the main character, Suenomori Yuta,</i>

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:37.740
<b>Suenomori Yuta
</b>Got another new character in MysClo's gacha!
 #MysticClockwork #MysClo

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.990
<b>Suenomori Yuta
</b> I got an SSR on the free roll too!
 My luck is on fire
 #MysticClockwork #MysClo

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:42.540
<i>managed to draw consecutive SSR characters.</i>

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:42.540
<b>Suenomori Yuta
</b> These great SSR rates...
 Are you guys not getting them?
 #MysticClockwork #MysClo #MysticClockwork #MysClo

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:42.540
<b>Suenomori Yuta
</b>I got another one...
 Am I using up a lifetime's 
worth of luck on this game????
 #MysticClockwork #MysClo

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:47.170
<i>This resulted in the already simmering 
resentment at the low SSR rates...</i>

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:48.670
<b>Kaze-san</b>

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:48.670
<b></b>Is this fraud?

00:17:47.810 --> 00:17:51.500
<i>mixing together with the persistent bugs 
to create a storm of discontent.</i>

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.090
<b>Usakichi</b>

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.090
<b></b>Celebs get special treatment.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:51.500
<b>Taiyoushin</b>

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:51.500
<b></b>Don't screw with gamers!

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:53.420
<b>Attraction Point Co. Ltd</b>

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:53.420
<b>An Apology and Update Regarding <i>Mystic Clockwork</i></b>

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:53.420
<i>And to make things worse...</i>

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:56.930
<b>It's very unfortunate that a certain number
 of malicious users are causing problems with the service,
 and the issue will be resolved in an update to the application.</b>

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:56.930
<i>The company totally blew it 
with their response.</i>

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:58.890
<i>Which led to a surge of complaints...</i>

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:03.100
<i>The app's currently undergoing 
an indefinite period of maintenance.</i>

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:04.690
<i>And to make things even worse...</i>

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:06.890
You have to do something, Kawasegawa-kun!

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:09.720
<i>The internally-developed engine that 
had been a potential problem from day one</i>

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:12.070
<i>was now a major problem.</i>

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:15.110
Sir, I already told you...

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:17.460
Unless we address the fundamental 
issues causing all this—

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:20.020
Well, we obviously can't do that 
at this stage, can we?!

00:18:20.020 --> 00:18:23.710
So you expect us to keep 
a house of cards from falling apart

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:26.750
with more temporary stopgap measures?!

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:27.990
Yes! Exactly!

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:30.000
We can't do anything else at this point!

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:41.590
Hashiba-san!

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:47.120
There's no stopping the train once its going!

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:49.480
That's the kind of business we're in!

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:50.230
I'm trying to say—

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:51.230
Enough already!

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:54.650
I don't care what kind of bull you 
have to spew. Just deal with it!

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:56.050
Hashiba-san!

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:57.440
I'm sorry...

00:18:57.440 --> 00:19:00.370
But there's nothing I can do.

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:06.960
It doesn't matter what comes later, 
so stop worrying about it.

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:06.780
<i>I decided not to make 
the same mistake again.</i>

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:09.990
Everything in this business 
comes down to speed and timing.

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:09.990
<i>So that I can protect this world.</i>

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:14.160
While we're having this chat, 
users are already ditching the service!

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:14.150
<i>Which is why... there's nothing I can do.</i>

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:15.890
Even if it ends up taking longer,

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.380
<b>An update for you... N@NA has posted a new video.</b>

00:19:15.890 --> 00:19:17.380
we'd be better off admitting our mistakes,

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:21.320
and prioritizing an effort to
 fix the underlying problems!

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:24.290
Pretending like we're fixing things when we're 
not while taking our audience for granted

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:26.970
will be the exact thing that makes 
people give up on this game!

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:28.220
<b>Excuse time!</b>

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:29.480
<b>Excuse time!</b>

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:32.090
<i>Hey there! It's N@NA!</i>

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:35.260
<i>Um... first, well...</i>

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:36.320
<i>I'm sorry!</i>

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:40.760
<i>I just said I was going to give up, 
yet here I am, posting again.</i>

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:42.670
<i>And with an original song!</i>

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:47.330
<i>Man, how long has it been 
since I uploaded something original?</i>

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:50.400
<i>Y'know, a long time ago, during college...</i>

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:53.540
<i>There was someone who told me to sing.</i>

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:57.670
<i>That was what set me 
down the road of singing.</i>

00:19:58.970 --> 00:20:01.890
<i>Yeah... it's his fault.</i>

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:04.180
<i>It's all his fault.</i>

00:20:04.860 --> 00:20:07.170
<i>But... because of him,</i>

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:10.330
<i>someone as unremarkable 
as me started singing!</i>

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:12.910
<i>I found something I could be serious about.</i>

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:15.740
<i>But I didn't keep at it...</i>

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:18.320
<i>I just relied on him, 
instead of working hard myself...</i>

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:21.820
<i>And the second he was gone, 
I started slacking.</i>

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:25.990
<i>I blamed it all on him, 
and wanted to give up.</i>

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:30.810
<i>But... I... even if it's only me...</i>

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:34.580
<i>I don't want to be the one 
who invalidates everything he did!</i>

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:39.210
<i>Which is why I'm going to 
be singing some more!</i>

00:20:58.310 --> 00:21:01.200
<i>I don't think what I did 
can ever be forgiven.</i>

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:02.530
<i>And yet...</i>

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:06.950
<i>In this world made by my own failings, 
I found some small salvation.</i>

00:21:07.930 --> 00:21:10.530
<i>Not from the popular singer, N@NA...</i>

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:13.200
<i>But Kogure Nanako was still singing...</i>

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:16.330
<i>She hadn't given up on the thing 
that she took seriously.</i>

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:20.710
<i>She blamed me... 
and said it was thanks to me.</i>

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:23.570
<i>And that I wasn't just meddling.</i>

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:28.880
<i>Thanks for listening all the way to the end!</i>

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:32.220
<i>Well, see you next time!</i>

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:35.510
I am the president of this company!

00:21:35.510 --> 00:21:36.640
It can't be done!

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:38.940
If we do that, it'll mean more bugs—

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:38.940
Thank you, Nanako.

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:40.480
There's nothing else we can do!

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:43.480
Now would you just do as I tell you?!

00:21:49.690 --> 00:21:52.670
<i>There's no way... there's </i>nothing<i>...</i>

00:21:53.110 --> 00:21:54.250
<i>that we can do!</i>

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:04.430
We're going to figure something out, damn it!
